# Every variable the app reads, with a safe placeholder or documented format — never a real
# value. This file is the contract; the typed env module is the enforcement. Keep the two in sync in the same PR that adds a variable, and group entries
# by concern with a one-line comment saying what breaks if the variable is wrong.

# --- App ---
# [VARIABLE]=[PLACEHOLDER OR FORMAT, e.g. http://localhost:3000]

# --- Database ---
# DATABASE_URL=[FORMAT, e.g. postgres://user:pass@localhost:5432/dbname]

# --- Auth ---
# [AUTH_SECRET]=[GENERATE PER ENVIRONMENT; never share between staging and prod]

# --- Third-party services ---
# [SERVICE_API_KEY]=[WHERE TO OBTAIN IT, and which tier/scopes it needs]
